2. `docs/paper/fable52-triage.md:16`, item 3: Qualify “X5-AG/v2 beats X7-SC … on fresh1-3” as a **training** comparison. On fresh2, X5-AG/v2 has lower evaluation gain: 0.072332 versus 0.072697. Its training selection does not establish higher evaluation gain on all three markets. The envelope calculation remains correct.

3. `docs/paper/fable52-triage.md:14`, item 1: Replace the doubled-search movement of `0.053` with `0.054`. The heldout gain changes by 0.053827; the stored training-profit change is 0.053930. Both round to 0.054. The margin-timing rebuttal is valid.

4. `main.tex:20–22`: Complete Fable’s requested abstract reduction. It still contains approximately 483 words and several unexplained codes. Keep four findings in plain language; move the search-family details and factorial contrast to the results. Removing the lottery sentence has not resolved this presentation issue.

