ft the lower gain; the other ten were not rechecked, and their stored development gains, all zero or below at the inner budget, are in the release; the two best were rechecked at full budget (runner-up C-thr($K = \const{12}$)), and the selected comparator is C$^* = $ C-mem($K = \const{6}$, $M = \const{20}$). C$^*$ is the best of four tested adaptations; it is not the strongest possible credibility rule, and R3 embodies earlier development choices that the comparison does not equalise. C$^*$/S0 is C$^*$ with B3's spread pacing.
 
